==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1 & 2'''===
This is a unique stage, in which a variety of peons spawn in mass numbers and there is no specific main threat. There is a restriction in place to not make this stage too easy. Bring any strong [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] (specifically [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris]]/[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama]] & [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway]] as they have adequate range) and [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]]. Meatshield when necessary. Some examples of meatshields are [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cats]] or [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan Cat]] due to their high health, [[Wave Attack]]s, speed or attack speed. Don't overdo it or else you'll hit the deploy limit and can't protect your existing cats.

Nearly any Area Attack [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] can help. Soon enough, you'll have enough attacking cats that you don't need meatshields at all. Just keep spamming those attackers.

Surge attackers help similarly. If one happens to have [[Brainwashed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Gross]] or any uber with surges, they can also obliterate the waves of peons, acting as a meat grinder that melts the miscellaneous enemies.

In Chapter 2, remember to bring a [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breaker]] for the UltraBaaBaas.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The general idea is to survive the long waves of Dark Doges, Gabriels, and both Mesocosmocyclones to win the stage. [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Neo Psychocat]], [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] are no-brainers against the Mesocosmocyclones for their respective [[Slow|slow]], [[Immune to Warp]] and [[Freeze|freeze]] abilities, while [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] is recommended to do the killing. If one happens to have [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]], they help massively against this stage due to their high-damage wave attacks clearing a majority of the peons.

